  <title id="bdl03coveragediagnostics-title">Coverage diagnostics: expected coverage and marginal simulation-based calibration</title>
  <desc id="bdl03coveragediagnostics-desc">Left, expected coverage based on the highest-probability density region: two observations x o 1 and x o 2 each give a posterior q of theta given x o, drawn as a shaded region with the true parameter theta star marked as a dot. Their results feed a plot of posterior coverage against nominal coverage, where the dashed diagonal is the ideal and a solid curve lies below it, with a double arrow marking the gap. Right, marginal simulation-based calibration: for each observation the posterior marginals of theta 1 and theta 2 are drawn as grey curves with the true value as a vertical line. Their ranks feed two plots of posterior rank: for theta 1, labelled calibrated, the curve follows the diagonal; for theta 2, labelled overconfident, the curve is S-shaped, above the diagonal at low ranks and below it at high ranks.</desc>
